# Rust
target/
crates/*/target/
desktop-client/src-tauri/target/

# Node
node_modules/
desktop-client/dist/
desktop-client/node_modules/

# Local configuration. .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.local

# Model weights and anything downloaded at install time. ANCHORED, and it has to
# stay that way: an unanchored `models/` matches at every depth, and because
# macOS sets core.ignorecase=true it matches `Models/` too -- which is a Swift
# source directory in apple-client. The bare pattern silently swallowed the
# entire wire-type layer: builds pass on the machine that wrote them and every
# clone fails to compile. Weights live under HEARTH_ROOT, which is backend/ in a
# checkout, so that is where the rule points.
/backend/models/
*.gguf

# Xcode. Nothing in this repository needed these until apple-client existed.
# They apply repo-wide on purpose: apple-client sits in this working directory
# even on branches that do not track it, so without them a DESKTOP commit
# sweeps up Xcode user state and the signing config -- which is how four such
# files reached a merge on 2026-08-08.
# Note what is NOT here: Package.resolved. The pinned revisions are the ones
# that build, and for a zero-dependency project it is a short file that usefully
# documents the absence.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcuserdatad
DerivedData/
.swiftpm/
apple-client/**/Local.xcconfig

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Native dev environments and fetched runtime binaries. The installer
# produces these on a user machine; a checkout produces them here.
backend/.venv-win/
backend/.native/

# Session ledgers the harness writes when HEARTH_ROOT is the checkout.
# FOLLOW-UP: state belongs under HEARTH_HOME, not the product tree.
backend/sessions/

# Packed by scripts/pack_backend.sh before every bundle build. Windows packs
# the .exe, macOS and Linux the bare binary; a checkout ignores whichever the
# machine it sits on produces.
desktop-client/src-tauri/resources/backend.tar.gz
desktop-client/src-tauri/resources/hearth-supervisor.exe
desktop-client/src-tauri/resources/hearth-supervisor
desktop-client/src-tauri/resources/tts-server
desktop-client/src-tauri/resources/tts-server.exe
desktop-client/src-tauri/resources/omnivoice-tts
desktop-client/src-tauri/resources/omnivoice-tts.exe

# The voice engine's pinned upstream checkout, cloned and patched by
# scripts/build_omnivoice.sh. Reproducible from the pin plus vendor/omnivoice,
# so the tree itself is build output.
.build/

# The by-hand startup proof: machine-specific script and its logs.
backend/.proof/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Icon workbench: build artifacts stay local.
design/icons/node_modules/
apple-client/**/.build/

# Folder grants written by the permission card. Whose machine holds which
# folders is the operator's business, not the product's.
backend/harness/valar/tools/file_grants.yaml
/releases/

# A persona's own memory (notes, activity log, session index, archive) is
# per-install state beside the manifest, never source.
backend/personas/*/memory/

# Agent configuration. The doc pipeline (orchestrator, researcher, author,
# reviewer) and its style skill are working tooling for whoever is editing the
# wiki, not part of the product a stranger installs. scripts/lint_wiki.py is
# deliberately NOT here: the linter is a guardrail the repository should carry.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Working clone used to push wiki/ to the GitHub wiki repository. Machine-local,
# and it holds its own .git.
.wiki-publish/

# Review artifacts written by the doc pipeline's reviewer stage. Scoring output
# for whoever ran it, not a wiki page.
wiki/**/*.review.json
